Open Tableau and connect to Superstore.csv.
Create a new worksheet.
Rename the worksheet Sales vs. Sales Forecast by State.
Drag Country to Filters.
Select United States only and click OK.
Drag Sales to Columns. Ensure it shows SUM(Sales).
Create a calculated field by clicking Analysis → Create Calculated Field.
Name the calculated field Avg_sale.
Enter this formula:
{ FIXED [State] : SUM([Sales]) }
Click OK.
Drag Avg_sale to Rows.
On the Marks card, select Circle.
Drag State to Color.
Drag State to Detail.
Adjust the view to Entire View if required.
Set the title to Sales vs. Sales Forecast by State.



Open Tableau and connect to Superstore.csv.
Create a new worksheet.
Rename the worksheet Profit Analysis by Sub-Category Over Time.
Drag Sub-Category to Columns.
Drag Ship Date to Columns, after Sub-Category.
Click the Ship Date pill dropdown and select Year.
Drag Profit to Rows. Ensure it shows SUM(Profit).
On the Marks card, select Circle.
Drag Sub-Category to Color.
If required, drag Sub-Category to Detail.
If your journal requires only 2012–2014, drag Ship Date to Filters and select those years.
Set the title to Profit Analysis by Sub-Category Over Time.


